srow(31, 1, 'MATERIAL', f'"HEAR, O ISRAEL: THE LORD OUR GOD, THE LORD IS ONE" (6:4) — WHY IS IT SAID? BECAUSE IT IS SAID "SPEAK TO THE CHILDREN OF ISRAEL" (EXODUS 25:2) — NOT "TO THE CHILDREN OF ABRAHAM", NOT "TO THE CHILDREN OF ISAAC": JACOB OUR FATHER MERITED THAT THE WORD BE SAID TO HIS SONS, FOR JACOB FEARED ALL HIS DAYS LEST WORTHLESS SEED GO OUT FROM HIM AS FROM HIS FATHERS — ISHMAEL FROM ABRAHAM (GENESIS 21:9 "PLAYING" READ AS IDOLATRY), THE WORDS OF R. AKIVA; R. SHIMON BEN YOHAI: FOUR THINGS R. AKIVA EXPOUNDED AND I EXPOUND THEM OTHERWISE — ISHMAEL AND ISAAC QUARRELLED OVER FIELDS AND VINEYARDS AND THE FIRSTBORN\'S DOUBLE SHARE. The head row of piska 31, THE FIRST PISKA ON THE CHAPTER ({SP_(31, 1, "זכה", "אבינו", "יעקב")} "Jacob our father merited"): the name "Israel" in 6:4 read as JACOB\'S OWN NAME — the creed addressed to Jacob\'s sons because the father feared for his seed; the row opens the four-fold dispute (31:1-4) of R. Akiva and R. Shimon ben Yohai on Ishmael\'s "playing", the quails, Ezekiel\'s "Abraham was one", the four fasts. The ink beside it: "hear, O Israel" four seats, all this book\'s (5:1, 6:4, 9:1, 20:3 — computed); the row cites 6:4 in both files ("(דברים ו ד)" — "Deuteronomy 6:4" — the head). The middah: a name\'s choice read as a pointer (E10\'s kin — "children of Israel" repeated against the absent "children of Abraham"); the SEAT for the claim DV06-02. Fresh in both files.')
srow(31, 2, 'CONTEXT', f'THE SECOND OF THE FOUR: "SHALL FLOCKS AND HERDS BE SLAIN FOR THEM" (NUMBERS 11:22) — R. AKIVA: WOULD IT SUFFICE THEM? R. SHIMON BEN YOHAI: EVEN ALL THE FLOCKS OF THE WORLD, THEY WOULD STILL MURMUR — AND THE HOLY SPIRIT ANSWERED "NOW YOU SHALL SEE" (11:23). The dispute\'s second exhibit ({SP_(31, 2, "כיוצא", "בו", "אתה", "אומר")} "in the same manner you say"); nothing on the chapter — the quails\' verse, Tosefta Sotah 6:7 in the English\'s note. Fresh.')
